{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>He and all the people who were with him.</b> It is written in the Book of the Wars of the Sons of Jacob that the neighbors of Shechem gathered together and waged three wars against them, and had not their father [Jacob] also girded his sword and his weapons of war and fought against them, they would have been in great danger. And so our Rabbis of blessed memory alluded to it regarding Jacob (Genesis 48:22): אשר לקחתי מיד האמורי בחרבי ובקשתי — which I took from the hand of the Amorite with my sword and with my bow — all those around them gathered to join battle against them, and Jacob girded his weapons of war against them. But the way of Scripture is to be brief in matters such as these, for it was a hidden miracle; and so Scripture was also brief regarding the matter of Abraham in Ur Kasdim, and likewise it did not mention at all the wars of Esau against the Horite sons here, and in order to make known this great hidden miracle Scripture mentioned <b>he and all the people who were with him</b>, to say that not a single one of them was missing in that great war."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:43.319948778Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}